GIMP Palette
Name: Shooter — Rust Belt Arena
Columns: 4
#
# Direction: a decommissioned foundry floor with the lights still on. Oil-dark
# ground, hazard paint that has not been repainted in years, machines that were
# never meant to be hostile.
#
# The arena is 2400x1600 and the camera is tight, so the player spends the whole
# game looking at ground. That is why tar-* is four steps of nearly nothing: it
# has to stay interesting across a screenful while never once competing with a
# threat. Everything dangerous is warm and everything inert is not.
#
# alarm-* exists because rust-* had to do two jobs it could not do at once —
# hazard stripes are decor and want to recede, an enemy about to reach you is
# not and must not.
#
 26  26  26	outline
 24  20  22	tar-0-pit
 46  40  38	tar-1
 74  64  58	tar-2
108  94  84	tar-3-rim
132  70  28	rust-1-shadow
188 106  36	rust-2
236 158  56	rust-3
255 214 120	rust-4-hilite
 40  54  68	steel-0-shadow
 78  98 120	steel-1
132 156 180	steel-2
206 224 240	steel-3-hilite
